I started to play tourist game. In dlvl 2 shop I found speed boots and
somewhere little later I got the shield of reflection. After I got
unholy water and cursed magic marker from bones and identified ring of
teleport control, I decided to make the game a 6-conduct run: atheist
wishless genocideless polysefless polypileless. The whole game was
going extremely well. Very soon I found and identified cursed scroll
of genocide, made gray dragon scale mail and cruisingly I reached the
Castle with my four pets Dawkins, Hitchens, Harris and Dennett. Most
powerful of them was Dawkins, who at XL 30 and over 200 HP ravaged
soldiers without breaking a sweat. One of the dragons in the armory
passage dropped uncursed +0 Grayswandir. I was overjoyed, as getting
good artifact weapon is impossible for atheist wishless player without
a stroke of luck and getting the best one is nothing short of miracle.
When I was embarking on the quest I was XL 13, but by luring the
wraiths out of Home level I was able to get XL 15. I was collecting
all the loot (to spare the only magic marker I had as much as
possible). I killed the Master of Thieves to his room, throwing potion
of paralysis at him and than whacking him to death. I had to
alternatively carry two bags of holding to be able to get all the loot
to Home level again. There I dropped both bags by the stairs and
talked to Twoflower. When he vacated the throne, I pulled out all
staff I hoped to get identified and sat on the throne. "Your mind
turns into pretzel. The throne vanishes in a puff of logic." Nah,
nothing -- as usual. But wait, why is Twoflower angry all of sudden?
Before I realized what went wrong, Twoflower expelled me out of quest
and removed the Quest portal. Bummer.

What happened was that I did not realize that the throne confused me
and tried to move away, accidentally attacking Twoflower. Now, my
situation is dire. All my belongings apart from things I keep in main
inventory are in the quest, including the Castle wand of wishing,
several wands of polymorph, extra magic lamp, all scrolls I ever had
and all potions. I have some limited stashes in the dungeon, with
nothing really too much useful -- I'll be lucky if I have left unholy
water somewhere.

My options now fork into two main branches:

1) I shall try to keep my conducts intact and thus write off all stuff
that was left in the Quest. I have the PYEC, the Grayswandir, +0 GDSM,
burnt speed boots and cursed magic lamp plus other sundry thing that
one keeps in inventory (luckstone, touchstone, unicorn horn, rings of
teleport control, levitation, slow digestion, regeneration, very few
wands). What I have lost is my only magic marker and all the scrolls
of enchant armor (my current AC is -5), plus sundry other stuff
(wands, potions, some extra items, all food).

2) I shall try to regain access to quest. Since the only way to do it
is to wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica, I would break the wishing
and artiwishing conducts. That of course under the condition that I am
able somehow able to find way to wish. I have cursed magic lamp, but I
don't have holy water and as an atheist, I don't have any means of
making it. The only way I can imagine at the moment is to farm for it
or hope to find some in the Gehennom.

What do now?
